{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":828,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.91","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 91","reference":"Psalms 91","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"This psalm is a dialogue, wherein one declares the safety of them, who take God for their keeper, ver."},{"verse":2,"text":"1."},{"verse":3,"text":"David declares this to be his resolution, ver."},{"verse":4,"text":"2."},{"verse":5,"text":"Various promises are made to him, ver."},{"verse":6,"text":"3-13."},{"verse":7,"text":"Which God himself confirms, ver."},{"verse":8,"text":"14-16."},{"verse":9,"text":"1.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"He - He that makes God his habitation and refuge.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":11,"text":"3.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"Pestilence - From the pestilence, which like a fowler's snare takes men suddenly and unexpectedly.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":13,"text":"5.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":14,"text":"By night - When evil accidents are most terrible and least avoidable.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":15,"text":"Arrow - The pestilence, or any such destructive calamity; such are frequently called God's arrows.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":16,"text":"By day - Thou shalt be kept from secret and open mischiefs.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":17,"text":"6.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":18,"text":"Darkness - Invisibly, so that we can neither foresee nor prevent it.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":19,"text":"12.","scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":20,"text":"Bear thee - Sustain or uphold thee in thy goings, as we do a child.","scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":21,"text":"13.","scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":22,"text":"The lion - Shall lie prostrate at thy feet, and thou shalt securely put thy feet upon his neck.","scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":23,"text":"Dragon - By which he understands all pernicious creatures, though never so strong, and all sorts of enemies.","scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":24,"text":"14.","scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":25,"text":"Because - This and the two following verses are the words of God.","scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":91}}